{{also|mahne}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|mane}}, from {{inh|de|goh|mana}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*manō||mane}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*mon-||neck}}. In Middle High German there existed a secondary variant {{m|gmh|man|g=m}}, whence the plural {{m|gmh|mene}}. The modern form {{m|de||Mähne}} is from this plural (or from its merger with the original form {{m|gmh||mane}}). Cognate with {{cog|en|mane}}, which see.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈmɛːnə/}} {{qualifier|standard; used naturally in western Germany and Switzerland}}
* {{IPA|de|/ˈmeːnə/}} {{qualifier|overall more common; particularly northern and eastern regions}}
* {{hyphenation|de|Mäh|ne}}
